ve up." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c011939a23a6e5d0debb54f085c155a61e7ae23ef2788846231114773e7b932"} {"question" "q-114060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A function $f(x)$ is concave up over an interval $(a,b)$ if ${f}^{″}(x)>0$ for all $x\\in (a,b).$\n\nOn the given graph of $y={f}^{″}(x),$ we can see that ${f}^{″}(x)>0$ on the intervals  $(-1,0)$ and  $(0,1).$  Therefore, the function $f(x)$ is concave up on the intervals  $(-1,0)$ and  $(0,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c011939a23a6e5d0debb54f085c155a61e7ae23ef2788846231114773e7b932"} {"question" "q-114060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6fe74a5f33fb1820ffabf22a6c87527c6ab012dbdae55ed8ef38b4201dc8ed8b"} {"question" "q-114060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c011939a23a6e5d0debb54f085c155a61e7ae23ef2788846231114773e7b932"} {"question" "q-114060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-\\infty ,0)"] ["math" "(0,1)"] ["math" "(0,\\infty )"] ["text" "$(-1,0)$ and  $(0,1)$"] ["text" "$(-\\infty ,-1)$ and  $(1,\\infty )$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14043400/state.json" "file_sha256" "1c011939a23a6e5d0debb54f085c155a61e7ae23ef278884623